    bc: Separate fatal diagnostic formatting from hot execution
    
    Mark numeric and VM fatal formatting as cold and non-inlined where the
    compiler supports those hints. Keep a noinline MSVC path and an ordinary
    noreturn fallback elsewhere. Runtime checks, source context, formatting,
    streams and exit status remain unchanged.
    
    Evaluate actual release code size and matched workloads before adopting
    this layout choice; formatting size alone is not a speed claim.
    
    All 212 unit cases (691942 assertions), eight CLI/helper groups and six
    malformed-offset groups pass in Release. Existing tests exercise semantic
    errors and checked execution without weakening their diagnostics.
    
    Refs #202 and #197.

